name: sim.checkOctreePointOccupancy
description: Checks whether the provided points collide with the OC tree voxels
luaSynopsis: int res, int tag, int locLow, int locHigh = sim.checkOctreePointOccupancy(int octreeHandle, int options, list points)
pythonSynopsis: int res, int tag, int locLow, int locHigh = sim.checkOctreePointOccupancy(int octreeHandle, int options, float[] points)
inputs:
1. octreeHandle: handle of the OC tree
2. options: bit-coded:
    - bit0 set (1): specified points are relative to the OC tree reference frame, otherwise they are relative to the world reference frame
3. points: points specified as x/y/z coordinates
outputs:
1. res: 0 if the points do not collide with the voxels, 1 if the points collide with the voxels
2. tag: tag value of the voxel that collides with a single point. If several points are tested, this return value should be ignored
3. loc: value specifying the location of the voxel that collides with a single point. If several points are tested, then this return value should be ignored
